```cpp
template <class Adaptor>
void Consensus<Adaptor>::timerEntry(
    NetClock::time_point const& now,
    std::unique_ptr<std::stringstream> const& clog)
{
    CLOG(clog) << "Consensus<Adaptor>::timerEntry. ";

    if (phase_ == ConsensusPhase::accepted) {
        CLOG(clog) << "Nothing to do during accepted phase. ";
        return;
    }

    now_ = now;
    CLOG(clog) << "Set network adjusted time to " << to_string(now) << ". ";

    auto const phaseOrig = phase_;
    CLOG(clog) << "Phase " << to_string(phaseOrig) << ". ";

    checkLedger(clog);

    if (phaseOrig != phase_) {
        CLOG(clog) << "Changed phase to << " << to_string(phase_) << ". ";
    }
}
```
- Logs entry into the function.
- If the consensus phase is `accepted`, it logs and returns immediately (no further action is needed until the next round).
- Updates the internal time (`now_`).
- Logs the current phase.
- Calls `checkLedger(clog)`, which is responsible for checking the current state of the ledger and possibly advancing the consensus phase, handling timeouts, or triggering other actions as needed.
- If the phase has changed as a result of `checkLedger`, it logs the new phase.

---

### 5. Summary of Logic

- **If consensus is already accepted:** Do nothing.
- **Otherwise:**
  - Update the internal time.
  - Log the current phase.
  - Call `checkLedger` to process the current state and possibly advance the consensus.
  - Log if the phase has changed.

---

### 6. Error Handling

- If a `SHAMapMissingNode` exception occurs during the consensus process, it is logged and rethrown.

---

### 7. Key Points

- The function is phase-aware and only acts if the consensus is not already accepted.
- The main logic for advancing the consensus process is encapsulated in `checkLedger`, which is called on each timer tick.
- All actions and phase changes are logged for debugging and monitoring.

---

